<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> History</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong></p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>It's a monastery that enlightens you.</li>
<li>The temple has strange effect on individuals that makes people self reflect on their current situation.</li>
<li>All individuals will go on their own journey towards enlightenment in the temple. Thought they may not know it.</li>
<li>In the end of their journey, an individual calling himself Brahma will give them two options: To surrender the enlightenment and leave forever, or to keep the enlightenment and stay to take care of the temple for the rest of their lives..</li>
<li>Those who become enlightened are declared denizens of the temple. All denizens have some sort of personality change though it varies from individuals.</li>
<li>Personality changes vary for several factors such as past experiences, ideals, and their own personal journey in the temple.</li>
<li>Those who decide to leave the temple are more likely to experience depression like symptoms.</li>
<li>Enlightenment, means different things to different people. This is the subject that I want this SCP to dive into.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>I will be exploring the monastery and its effects on individuals by using testimonies of several residents and people who work on the site</strong></p>
<p>Resident Responsibilities<br />
◾They protect, clean, and maintain the temple.<br />
◾The rooms they take care of includes, the farm, the library, front desk, springs.<br />
◾It's important to maintain, the temple in order to keep the temple effects.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative will follow the first researcher of the temple Dr.Weddell. As his story progresses the reader will learn more about the temple, as he slowly is affected by the temple. The reader will realize what the enlightenment is along will the doctor. Dr.Weddell is a man with troubled past and because of the temples abtilty to make one reflect on their situation. This bring forth the negative side of the SCP, because the enlightenment can be forth a positive change or a negative change. Sadly, Dr.Wedell is experiencing a negative change which lead Dr.Wedell to a sad end.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> If their is a part of the greenlight, you are unsure about, please contact me, because I do have so information I couldn't place on the greenlight due to word count limit.</p>

