<p>Heyo follow-up!</p>
<p><strong>~Some stuff~</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
<strong>The concept:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Elevator Pitch:</p>
<p>It's a monastery( or Temple) that enlightens you.<br />
This temple answers only the question that your heart yearns for.<br />
Their is this room called &quot;The room of enlightenment&quot; where a mysterious individual will answer your question.<br />
Enlightenment, means different things to different people. This is the subject that I want this SCP to dive into.<br />
Their are monks their that take care of the Temple, and the Foundation and the Monks reached a agreement in order study this SCP.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This looks a little more developed than before, but I'm still not particularly hooked on the idea. You seem to have some ideas here that either aren't explored or given enough detail, or ideas that don't seem to be brought up again. My most prominent examples being the &quot;mysterious individual&quot; and the monks themselves.-these elements sound important to the skip, but they don't seem to be brought up again?</p>
<p>Overall, I would recommend you step back from the smaller details and look at everything objectively. Really get to know the skip itself, and how everything functions. Some examples: What do these monks do? why/how is this important to the monasteries upkeep? is there any history behind the 'mysterious individual'? does he/she have any established motives?</p>
<p>In general, I would recommend you let yourself experiment with the idea, often times you may find the concept builds itself as you introduce new ideas or storylines.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sadly the effects of SCP has negative effects on the mental health and physical health of all involved. The side effects may include<br />
Shorter lifespan<br />
Sudden seizures<br />
Schizophrenia<br />
Muscles loss<br />
loss in vision to one or both eyes<br />
Their will several logs going thought several peoples journey for enlightenment, of several different people. Each person will go through their own journeys for enlightenment, which all lead to this SCP. But instead stating a true answer in this article I will let the readers come to their own conclusion to what enlightenment is. Just like characters do.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure if I'm too on board with this part, it feels a bit disconnected from the rest of the concept and the effects shown here feel like a way to grab attention and sounds scary.</p>
<p>From what I can see, your plan is for the audience to get gradually more interested in this 'enlightenment' as the article progresses. This isn't a bad concept by any means, though as it stands the enlightenment doesn't grab my attention.</p>
<p><strong>A recommendation, along with an idea I got while typing:</strong></p>
<p>(<strong>don't</strong> feel the idea needs to be taken seriously)</p>
<p>-I would recommend linking the 'enlightenment' back to the monastery (the current effects don't give me much insight into anything, they don't make me as reader want to learn more).</p>
<p>perhaps the people seeking this &quot;enlightenment&quot; end up becoming residents? committing the rest of their lives to the monasteries upkeep.</p>
<p>And if you want to add a more grotesque spin to this, then perhaps they remove all sensory organs after they have been enlightened, though still functioning like normal (able to hear, touch, see ect.), though with no visible way of breathing, eating ect.</p>
<p><strong>The narrative:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Central Narrative: The story content will mostly consist of how the foundation came into custody of this SCP, and the agreement between the foundation and the Monks. Of course first the foundation will try to take this SCP into custody by force, but after failing to take over the Monastery multiple times. The foundation came to an agreement with the monasteries residents.</p>
<p>The agreement is as follows</p>
<p>The foundation is allowed to run test, but have to accompanied by two residents<br />
The monastery is allowed to remain open, but their has to 10 foundation personnel present and 10 residents president as well.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There still isn't much of a setup, middle act or payoff here. I'm not sure how the Foundation found the skip to begin with, why they decided to take the monastery by force (presumably without knowing anything before hand), how/when they came to the agreement, what was tested, what was learnt by the end and how the characters' stories fit with the Foundations.</p>
<p>As it stands, the story feels quite vague and barebones, as the events and characters are fairly vague. Though my biggest issue here lies with the lack of a strong conflict/twist, the whole story seems focused on this agreement, but that alone doesn't keep my interest and attention.</p>
<p>Considering you want the audience to be hooked on the enlightenment aspect, I would recommend you make that focus of the story. Show us the people who have gone through the process and what ends up happening to them, do any researchers, D-class or guards end up getting enlightened? what will make me as reader care about the characters (or the Foundation)? what do the tests teach us about the monastery? ect.</p>
<p><strong>Red or green?</strong><br />
For now I'll hold off on a greenlight, as the concept and story are still a little bland to me.- The effects feel a little disjointed and unrelated to the skip, and the story feels a bit anti-climatic/flat, as there isn't much to go off or get invested in.</p>
<p>That said, feel free to shoot me a PM if/when you would like more feedback or advise.</p>
<p>-Do note that if you're looking for additional critiques in general, then I would highly recommend the butterfly squad.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Cheers,</p>
<p>-The Desert</p>

