<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm gonna tell you straight up, I don't really like ideas with thaumiel potential, which is what your idea is right here. There are no apparent downsides to the temples effect, the residents there are cooperative with the foundation, etc; In my opinion, it makes for a really uninteresting article. For an example of a balanced narrative, take <a href="/scp-606">SCP-606</a>. The creature is a benevolent creature that only wishes to educate humans on the universe's vast expanse of knowledge, but unfortunately murders them in the process because the human brain simply can't take that level of information. Once you have this down, I think you'll find it much easier to come up with a much more involved and interesting narrative.</p>
