<p>Here to provide resources post-PM.</p>
<p>Hey <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/negative360" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6226240); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6226240&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1602529281" alt="Negative360" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6226240)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/negative360" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6226240); return false;">Negative360</a></span>, I hear your having a little trouble thinking of ideas to make your post better. First off, I suggest looking at the article <a href="/ideation">Ideation</a>. It's a great article to practice developing ideas, and I think it could help you a lot. Do a little brainstorming, try mixing ideas, basically do what the article tells you for about 10 minutes. Then you say &quot;Okay, now why does this idea matter? Why should the Foundation care? Why should I care? Why should the audience care?&quot;. Answering these questions is a crucial part of designing a narrative. Last of all, you need a hook to draw people in.</p>
<p>For instance, let's say I make a concept about a cartoon raccoon that can travel through broken television and steal old VCR's from out of tape recorders. The hook would be that if you get within 1 foot of the TV while the raccoon is there, a giant cartoon bear enters frame, reaches out and grabs you, and the TV turns off.</p>
<p>Let me know if this didn't help, or you need more resources.</p>
<p>EDIT: Came back to take a look at this article while scrolling through my PM's, noticed you had added some interesting changes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Below I will list some characters and their journey's, I will put in the logs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would recommend scrapping this, it doesn't really have any relevance unless the character significantly clarifies or changes views on the SCP.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But in exchange, you can not leave the temple, and you have to dedicate the rest of your life to the upkeep of the monastery.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I kind of like this idea, but it needs more explanation. How else does this change the victims? Are they entered into a vow of silence, or do they form a hive mind? If so, is this optional or forced? How do the indoctrinated subjects react to the Brahma or SCP personnel? Again, needs more expansion.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Enlightenment, means different things to different people. This is the subject that I want this SCP to dive into.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a great core concept, would love some more demonstration of it. Maybe diary entries or test logs, perhaps even brain wave scans of affected individuals? I like it, but don't really have a full picture.</p>
<p>Overall, this idea has improved massively, but still needs some work. Let me know if you need any help.</p>
<p>Your local conspiracy theorist, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/conspiracymirrorist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6797897); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6797897&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1602529281" alt="ConspiracyMirrorist" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6797897)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/conspiracymirrorist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6797897); return false;">ConspiracyMirrorist</a></span></p>

