<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My concern is that you seem focused on describing the characteristics and properties of the temple instead of telling a story.</p>
<p>I would suggest to focus on the researcher being influenced by the temple, Maybe you could tell the story of how the temple was discovered by the Foundation, they assigned a researcher, and we start to learn about the temple's properties alongside the researcher? Maybe some type of journal/notes/report detailling all their progress while they're being influenced?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Enlightenment, means different things to different people. This is the subject that I want this SCP to dive into.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You should write some testimonies in order to tell what &quot;Enlightenment&quot; means to some of the residents. But I think you should keep this part only to familiarize the reader with the &quot;Enlightenment&quot;. Also, I think the researcher's story could help the reader to know how this &quot;Enlightenment&quot; works its way into the person since the very beginning.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The residents , and the Foundation reached an silent agreement that is not currently in writing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The agreement should be written at least to know what they agreed upon. The residents of the temple might haven't signed it, but Foundation personnel should write that they agreed on something.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I think this would make a weird religious-esque article, but it'll be interesting.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>
